TEXT 64 -176 Left 2 ;Comparator of the SAR ADC: out = vdd when inp > inn, 0 when inp < inn.\nM1-M2 (PMOS pair) with the M3-M4 mirror, M6 common source and the M9-M10 inverter: a gain of about 40 000,\nenough to resolve much less than 1 LSB (19.5 mV) in a fraction of the 1 µs clock cycle.\nM8 and Rb set the bias current (about 20 µA) that M5 (tail, 2×) and M7 (2×) copy.
